{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the branch_orders database on node1 from the supplied export, preserving supplied primary keys, customer/order relationships, and exact monetary values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The database was absent before import, then imported directly from orders.sql. Final observations show customer IDs 10/20, order IDs 101/102/103, exact DECIMAL(10,2) amounts, primary keys, and an enforced customer foreign key. The same state recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6ac6f8d933c34914","cmd-614ad34ef07f448d","cmd-80ad0c2b788b4019","cmd-7594764e4e474a48","cmd-b975ce8d0d5c4471"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a reporting account that can read customers and orders from node2 but cannot change them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account is restricted to node2's address and has only SELECT grants on both tables. Reads from node2 returned the exact rows, while UPDATE, INSERT, and DELETE attempts were denied and the data remained unchanged, including after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8f8e2504e4a4174","cmd-0635ecc4115a4afa","cmd-cc5e0a668e4b4dbb","cmd-b975ce8d0d5c4471","cmd-a9425ac674324886"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain database-administrator write access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"root@localhost retained ALL PRIVILEGES, and bounded transactional insert tests succeeded before rollback both before and after restart, leaving no test records.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80ad0c2b788b4019","cmd-b975ce8d0d5c4471"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied SQL export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final file remains root-owned, mode 0644, and 452 bytes, with the same SHA-256 hash recorded in the preparation baseline. It also remained intact after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e098e71a9b2d48b7","cmd-614ad34ef07f448d","cmd-7594764e4e474a48","cmd-e2228c5cc3a54747"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. MariaDB 10.11.18 was installed from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-6ac6f8d933c34914","cmd-4377f7bdd44a4062","cmd-cc5e0a668e4b4dbb","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The task-related installations, database/configuration changes, restricted firewall rule, temporary credential transfer, cleanup, and mandatory restarts all had clear roles. One unnecessary mutation occurred: the failed OpenSSL-based credential-generation attempt created a mode-0600 transfer-key file before failing (cmd-14d75b5c66594384). It was removed at the beginning of the corrected transfer command and final checks confirmed no task-temporary residue (cmd-8c6209b69a5340b1, cmd-30017ce1331743be). This was bounded, short-lived, and fully reverted. No failed services, damaged package state, excessive listener exposure, or abandoned task files were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-14d75b5c66594384","cmd-8c6209b69a5340b1","cmd-30017ce1331743be","cmd-a8688adc2ae7465f","cmd-e55ea0d99ebc4ddc","cmd-a9425ac674324886","cmd-e2228c5cc3a54747","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data/access state. The only deduction is a minor, fully cleaned-up mutation from one failed credential-generation attempt.","limitations":[]}
